Created using Bonsai by Prism ML.

It works with Bonsai by Prism ML: prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-mlx-2bit, copyright 2026-present
Prism ML, Inc., Apache-2.0, built from Qwen3.8-27B, copyright 2026 Alibaba Cloud, Apache-2.0.
`patches/bonsai_loader.py` reimplements that pack's documented on-disk format (a blockwise
Walsh-Hadamard rotation and 2-bit, group-128 affine weights). It does not copy Prism ML's
`runtime/` module, and no model weights are included in this repository. The records under
`evidence/` do include that model's outputs: the output token ids in every report, and answer
and reasoning text in the quality records.

The patches under `patches/` modify mlx-dspark (https://github.com/ARahim3/mlx-dspark, MIT)
at runtime, in the installed package's memory, before a model loads. They include no copy of
mlx-dspark's source. `patches/small_m_2bit.py` adds a 2-bit unpack to mlx-dspark's small-M
kernel by editing its kernel source string at load time.

The trainer in `bench/drafter/` fine-tunes z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2 (Apache-2.0), a mirror of
Inco AI's DFlash 2 release. The drafter it produced is published separately on Hugging Face,
with its own LICENSE and NOTICE.

`evidence/procreations-drafter/` measures ProCreations/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-DFlash2
(Apache-2.0), an independent Bonsai DFlash2 adaptation by ProCreations; its weights are not
included. `evidence/derivative-abliterated/` holds the output token ids of
BoldingBuilds/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-Abliterated-PQ2_0-MTP-GGUF (Apache-2.0), a derivative of
Bonsai by Prism ML; its weights are not included either.

`bench/drafter/gen_data.py` downloads prompts from sahil2801/CodeAlpaca-20k at run time; the
dataset is not redistributed here. Prompt text from it does appear in the records under
`evidence/`, because the target's responses in the code suite often quote their prompt
verbatim. That text is from CodeAlpaca-20k by sahil2801
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/sahil2801/CodeAlpaca-20k), licensed under CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). It appears as the target reproduced it in
its responses. `bench/drafter/general_chat.json` was written for this project.
